messages:
lucy: Heads up — product + runtime sync on the token-cost dashboard signals. want to align on what runtime/infra emits vs what console should compute. goal: single 1k-token cost view with cache/batch savings broken out per route/model/tenant.

kevin: +1. my main ask: keep the runtime output minimal (pre-agg counters) so we don't ship lots of raw event traffic. we can do joins in the metrics pipeline.

maria: We need the console to show both gross token spend and net (after cache + batch). PM questions: which breakdowns matter for customers? i care about by-route, by-model, and quantization-profile.

jordan: runtime can emit these three per-request deltas: tokens_requested, tokens_served_from_kv_cache, batching_savings_tokens. emitting per-request helps for accuracy but is heavier. alternative: a kumo counter that increments per-commit with tags.

ada?: (quick) is ada on this thread?

ada: i'm here — from SRE side we prefer pre-aggregated counters to avoid cardinality explosion. also want an error tag if fallback routing happened (so cost spike attribution doesn't blame main model).

kevin: proposal: runtime emits lightweight counter increments with these tags: model, route, tenant_id, quant_profile, routing_tier, fallback=true|false. counters: token_request_total, token_cache_hit_total, token_batch_savings_total.

lucy: that covers ownership but we also need a canonical event schema so telemetry team can backfill historic data. jordan, can runtime add proto and a small compatibility shim?

jordan: yes. i'll open a PR with a schema like below and a migration plan for 30d backfill. will add sampling for very high-traffic tenants.

```
# telemetry proto (sketch)
message TokenCostSignal {
  string tenant_id = 1;
  string model = 2;
  string route = 3;
  string quant_profile = 4;
  string routing_tier = 5;
  bool fallback = 6;
  int64 tokens_requested = 7;
  int64 tokens_cache_hit = 8;
  int64 tokens_batch_saved = 9;
  int64 ts = 10;
}
```

kevin: + comments: make route optional for legacy calls; also add api_key_id hashed for owner mapping.

maria: for the dashboard UX: can we show both absolute token savings and % savings side-by-side? also add a small explainer tooltip on how batch savings are estimated.

ada: addendum — quotas: if we start publishing net tokens to billing signals we must ensure quota enforcement still uses gross tokens_requested. don't want customers throttled incorrectly.

lucy: good call. plan: billing gets gross tokens, cost dashboard computes net tokens = tokens_requested - tokens_cache_hit - tokens_batch_saved. we'll label both metrics clearly.

telemetry-bot: new ticket created: METR-4823 'Token cost signals: counters + proto + dashboard wireframe' assigned to jordan, kevin, maria.

kevin: action items TL;DR — jordan: proto + runtime shim PR by EOD Wed; kevin: add tags to counter emitters + docs; maria: dashboard wireframe and tooltip copy by next Tue; lucy: coordinate backfill window and cross-team signoff; ada: validate quota separation and fallback tag semantics.

maria: one more — for canary/rollouts UI, add a toggle to view cost delta for a specific rollout cohort (canary vs baseline). useful when rolling quantization or new kernels.

jordan: noted, will include a canary_id tag on emits for 1 week after rollout if present. sampling rules will keep vol low.

lucy: perfect. i'm going to create a short shared doc with the schema, dashboard mock, and migration plan. tagging folks in that doc. thanks all :thumbsup:

kevin: thanks. if anyone wants early access to raw counters stream ping me and i'll open a read-only role.

ada: tiny follow-up — let's also add an alert if token_batch_savings drops >50% for a top-10 route; could be regression signal.

lucy: added as an item. end of thread.
